            <ArticleTitle>Incidence of postdural puncture headache. A prospective study of 101 spinal anaesthetics in orthopaedic patients.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>20-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>Spinal anaesthesia was performed on 101 patients with a 25-Gauge (0.52 mm) needle. We found a 13.9% overall incidence of postdural puncture headache (PDPH) in an orthopaedic population whose mean age was 33.6 years. This incidence is too high and an alternative technique may be needed.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
